= Ecosystem — Simple =

An '''ecosystem''' is a group of living things together with the soil, water, air, light and other conditions around them.

A pond, forest or coastal tide pool can be studied as an ecosystem. Plants and algae capture energy, animals eat food, and decomposers help return nutrients.

Energy moves through living things and is eventually transferred as heat. Materials such as carbon can cycle between organisms and their environment.

The boundaries of an ecosystem depend on what scientists are studying.

